WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.000
Good morning, John.

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:07.800
As I make this video, there are lots of people killing lots of people in France; in Paris.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.940
It is impossible for me to think about anything except for that thing;

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:13.160
and it is
also impossible for me to have any -

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:19.400
anything except feelings. Like, there's a time for analysis, there's a time for

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:25.369
thinking, there's a time for trying to figure out why people... are the way they are.

00:00:25.369 --> 00:00:34.200
Uh... where... behaviours originate. But, this is
not that time.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:38.390
It is just.. emotions. It is just sad,

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:40.200
fear, anger.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:44.700
I have a friend who's in Paris right now. He hasn't.. tweeted anybody;

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:48.700
he hasn't done anything on social media, so it's just terrifying.

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:55.870
It is just a time for.. feeling. Umm.. and I know that we all want to analyze, now we are

00:00:55.870 --> 00:01:01.300
living that kind of world where we want to immediately take our worldview and say:

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:10.260
"If only we had been the way we
should have been, the way that I wish the world were,

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:11.500
this wouldn't have happened."

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:19.700
That's going to be flawed forever. But it is especially flawed right now.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:25.000
And I think the thing to feel is.. wha- like, whatever it is we should feel.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:30.700
Like, you know, I think if the response is to disengage, that is appropriate.

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:37.000
If your response is to stare at live feeds from Twitter and Reddit, that is appropriate.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:45.649
If your response is to just be terrified for your friends, your family,

00:01:45.649 --> 00:01:53.170
yourself, or just people, because we are all people, that is appropriate.

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:54.400
There's nothing useful I could say.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.500
There's you know, like

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:00.300
"Hatred is not the correct response to hatred"..?

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:01.000
I don't know...

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:04.000
"The world is broken,
but hope is not crazy"..?

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:04.700
Yeah..?

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:07.500
That's good, that was a John Green one.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.500
It`s hard enough to think about the effects this kinda have like, globally and

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:11.500
on Europe..

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.500
It's hard not to
think about the effect that this is gonna have like globally and..and on Europe; but I just think like, right
now, I'm.. I want to think about the people... who risked their lives to save people.. and to help
people. I want to think about the people who've lost people. And I want to think about the people who've been lost. I think that's the thing to think about.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.500
That is the - yeah...

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.000
John, I will see you on Monday.

